CURL.EXE: curl 8.23.0 (https://curl.se, curl license) for DOS, on vmdos's
own TCP. HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, FTPS and FILE; TLS 1.2 and 1.3 by mbedTLS 3.6,
WGET's configuration (third_party/wget) with stdio buffering kept on
(curl_mbedtls_config.h: unbuffered, DJGPP read the CA bundle a byte at a
time, a DOS call each, and servers gave up waiting). Certificates are
checked against C:\VMDOS\NET\CACERT.PEM (third_party/cacert).

curl's DOS code is Watt-32's: dos/curl-dos.c gives it the Watt-32 calls it
makes (select_s, close_s, ioctlsocket) and recv/send on ssh's socket layer
(third_party/openssh/dos-sock.c), which talks to vmdos's TCP; the clock
reads DOS's date and time (dos/curl-dos.h, included first everywhere), as
ssh's does: DJGPP's gettimeofday() can hang under vmdos. curl_config.h is
the configuration, by hand (CMake isn't run): written from a CMake
configuration of the same features, and checked by building curl with it
as a 32-bit Linux program (same type sizes) and downloading over verified
HTTPS, chunked, and with redirects. mbedtls-alt.c gives mbedTLS entropy
and milliseconds.

Build: tools/build-curl.sh writes bin/CURL.EXE; the Makefile puts it in
C:\VMDOS\NET when it's there. DJGPP is a cross gcc on PATH, or else the
djfdyuruiry/djgpp Docker image, as for WGET.
